   - **FOOD LANE (below the axis, vertically aligned to the same months):** three macro segments at their stated proportions — `LEAN-BULK ~75%` (the wide growth slab) · `CUT ~20%` · `MAINTENANCE ~5%` (the thin bridge). Inside the bulk: an **8-week continuation-check tick** (`holding ~0.5%/wk = mostly muscle → continue; faster = mini-cut 2–4 wk`). Inside the cut: **refeed ticks** (single high-carb days) and two longer **diet-break** bars. A one-line coupling note between the lanes: `food is the lever you pull most — the drug lever only when extra food turns to FAT.`
5. **THE BODY-FAT GATE TRACE (threaded through both lanes — the load-bearing rule made geometric):** a single continuous trace running left→right, bounded by two horizontal reference lines: a **green push-band** `8–12% = grow here` and a hard **ceiling line** `~15% = never surplus above this`. The trace rises through the bulk, gets cut back down, rises again — always staying inside the band. At one point (over a sloppy-surplus stretch) it **pokes above the ceiling into the single RED ZONE** labelled `MICHELIN-MAN BREACH · insulin sensitivity craters · the surplus now HINDERS muscle` — the one red object on the poster, an envelope-breach, not a free-floating warning. Pull-back arrow drags it back under the line `cut at ~15–17%`.
