7. **DIAGNOSTIC CHECKPOINT FLAGS (small flags pinned along the year axis at ~3-month intervals):** `BLOODS q3 months` with the marker hierarchy compressed onto the flag stack — `Cystatin C (true GFR in muscular people) · ALT/AST (7-day no-train rule) · thyroid triad (GH speeds T4→T3) · SHBG (carrier, not enemy) · prolactin / cortisol`. Law plate beside them: `blood work is the final arbiter — a marker deviates, the cycle bends or stops, regardless of the mirror.`
